cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use adaptiveNet in academic, teaching, or published work, please cite it as below."
title: adaptiveNet
abstract: >-
  An interactive browser-based playground for node-edge dynamical systems
  where node states and connection topology coevolve. Includes Hopfield
  memory, spiking neurons, Ising spins, reaction-diffusion, voter dynamics,
  and self-organised criticality as instances of one substrate.
authors:
  - family-names: TT1nKer
    alias: TT1nKer
type: software
repository-code: "https://github.com/TT1nKer/adaptiveNet"
url: "https://tt1nker.github.io/adaptiveNet/"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - agent-based modeling
  - network dynamics
  - adaptive networks
  - reaction-diffusion
  - Hopfield network
  - spiking neurons
  - self-organised criticality
  - Ising model
  - interactive simulation
  - browser-based simulation
